.TH mkPreparedSource 5 "2026-07-24" "go-nix-helpers" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
mkPreparedSource \- private Go dependency injection for Nix sandbox builds
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
mkPreparedSource = import (go-nix-helpers + "/mkPreparedSource.nix") {
  inherit pkgs lib;
  goPkg = pkgs.go_1_26;
};

preparedSrc = mkPreparedSource {
  name = "my-app";
  src = ./.;
  deps = {
    "github.com/larsartmann/go-cqrs-lite" = inputs.go-cqrs-lite;
  };
};
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkPreparedSource
solves the problem of building Go projects that depend on private GitHub
modules inside the Nix sandbox. The Nix sandbox has no SSH and no network
access, so Go cannot fetch private dependencies.
.PP
This helper works by:
.IP 1. 3
Copying each dependency source into a
.I _local_deps/
directory within the build source
.IP 2. 3
Auto-discovering all sub-modules at any depth in the dependency tree
.IP 3. 3
Injecting
.B replace
directives into
.B go.mod
pointing to the local copies
.IP 4. 3
Stripping stale absolute and relative replace directives
.IP 5. 3
Validating that every private
.B require
has a matching
.B replace
.SH PARAMETERS
.TP
.BR name " (str, required)"
Derivation name prefix.
.TP
.BR src " (path, required)"
Source derivation or path containing the Go module.
.TP
.BR deps " (attrs, required)"
Attrset of { "import/path" = flake-input; }.
Each value must be a path to the dependency source.
.TP
.BR version " (str, default: \"dev\")"
Version string.
.TP
.BR autoSubModules " (bool, default: true)"
Auto-discover sub-modules from dep source trees.
When true, recursively walks each dep to find all go.mod files.
.TP
.BR excludeSubModuleDirs " (list str, default: [example examples testdata .git vendor node_modules])"
Directory names to skip during recursive auto-discovery.
.TP
.BR subModules " (attrs, default: {})"
Explicit sub-modules (merged with auto-discovered).
Keys are module paths, values are lists of relative paths.
.TP
.BR requireDeps " (attrs, default: {})"
Manually inject require lines into go.mod.
Rarely needed.
.TP
.BR subModuleVersion " (str, default: \"v0.0.0\")"
Version for pseudo-version normalization.
.TP
.BR stripLocalReplaces " (bool, default: true)"
Strip stale replace X => /home/... directives.
Covers absolute (/...), relative (./...), and sibling (../...) paths.
.TP
.BR validatePrivateDeps " (bool, default: true)"
Verify every private require in go.mod has a matching replace.
Fails the build with a clear error if validation fails.
.TP
.BR privateDepPattern " (str, default: \"github\\\\.com/[Ll]ars[Aa]rtmann/\")"
ERE regex matching private module paths to validate.
Override for other organizations.
.TP
.BR publicDeps " (list str, default: [])"
Module paths to exclude from private validation.
Use for repos that match privateDepPattern but are actually public.
Versioned-path aware: base path also matches /v2, /v3, etc.
.TP
.BR postPatchExtra " (str, default: \"\")"
Additional shell commands appended to postPatch.
Runs BEFORE replace directives are injected.
.SH EXCLUDED DIRECTORIES
The auto-discovery excludes the following directory names:
.BR example ,
.BR examples ,
.BR testdata ,
.BR vendor ,
.BR .git ,
.BR node_modules .
.SH /vN HANDLING
Major version suffixes (/v2, /v3, etc.) are handled correctly:
.IP \(bu 3
The version suffix is stripped from the local directory path
(e.g. event/v3/eventtest becomes event/eventtest)
.IP \(bu 3
The full versioned module path is kept in the replace directive
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Basic usage:
.nf
preparedSrc = mkPreparedSource {
  name = "my-app";
  src = ./.;
  deps = {
    "github.com/larsartmann/go-cqrs-lite" = inputs.go-cqrs-lite;
  };
};
.fi
.TP
With explicit sub-modules only:
.nf
preparedSrc = mkPreparedSource {
  name = "my-app";
  src = ./.;
  deps = { ... };
  autoSubModules = false;
  subModules = {
    "github.com/larsartmann/go-cqrs-lite" = [ "codec/v2" ];
  };
};
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR go-standard (5),
.BR nix (1),
.BR go (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Lars Artmann <https://github.com/LarsArtmann>
